"## Screen: 1af9df42-74ad-4c9c-af09-6abed26c80a0\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **Page URL**: https://app.attio.com/referodesign/reports/dashboard/73cda6b7-23ce-4a7f-9542-a15f25c6b464/cell/c35cbd6d-56dc-4b35-a51a-11417548d891/edit\n- **Preview URL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/attio.com/desktop/f62f29ce-fc70-4ae7-bd60-1108a185e1ab_preview.jpg\n- **Thumbnail URL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/attio.com/desktop/9d52c465-226d-4ac4-a0d5-8523b24f0aa8_thumb.jpg\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/1af9df42-74ad-4c9c-af09-6abed26c80a0\n- **UI Elements**: Search Field, Icon, Popover\n- **Fonts**: Inter, Intercom\n- **Colors**: 0x353637, 0xF2F3F4, 0x2B6CF3, 0x838EA6, 0xA5A4A4\n\n### Content\n- **Description**: The screen displays a data analytics dashboard focusing on report generation and visualization. The overall style is clean and professional with a white background (#FFFFFF) that enhances readability and clarity. The main section centers on a bar chart titled 'Companies by Country Count,' featuring vertical bars in a solid blue color (#2F79F5) with rounded corners and no gradients. The chart's axes are labeled with light gray lines (#CCCCCC) and numeric values (0.0 to 4.0) along the y-axis. The x-axis labels are simple numeric categories (1 to 5) with medium gray text (#666666), center-aligned. Above the chart, there is a header with the report title in a bold sans-serif font (likely 16px, weight 600). To the right of the title, a 'Refresh data' link is present in medium blue (#3A86FF), indicating interactivity upon hover (underline or color change not visible but typically expected). The right sidebar features form controls with dropdown menus for 'Data Source,' 'Report type,' and 'X axis' in a clean sans-serif font (14px, regular). The dropdown menus have subtle borders (#DDDDDD) and rounded corners with a light background (#F9F9F9). The 'X axis' dropdown is expanded, showing selectable company attributes like 'Domains,' 'Name,' 'Description,' etc., each with small icons and hierarchical submenus indicated by arrows. On the left, there's a vertical navigation sidebar with simple text links and icons, categorizing sections like Notifications, Tasks (with a blue badge indicating 2 tasks), Notes, Emails, Reports, Automations, Records, and Lists. The sidebar's background is light gray (#F5F5F5); the active or selected item ‘Companies’ is highlighted with a blue dot and slightly darker text (#2F79F5). At the bottom of the sidebar, there are small buttons for inviting teammates, accessing help, and a call-to-action button 'Add billing' in bright blue (#2F79F5) with white text. The layout uses spacing and padding effectively, with consistent margins around elements (about 16 to 24px), two main columns (sidebar left about 240px wide, main content area with chart flexible), and a right panel about 300px wide for controls. Typography is modern and simple, supporting usability and visual hierarchy. Icons are minimalist line icons consistent throughout. No visible animations, but dropdown interactions are implied. The header includes a small user avatar in the top right corner for account access. The interface is designed for clear data insight, easy filtering, and report configuration.\n- **Layout**: The layout is a three-column structure with a fixed vertical sidebar on the far left, a central main content area, and a right sidebar for settings and filters. The left column (sidebar) width is approximately 240px, containing navigation links grouped into sections with clear spacing and small icons aligned left of the text. The center column contains the report title at the top, followed by the bar chart below, with generous padding (about 24px) around elements for readability. The right column is about 300px wide, dedicated to data source selection, report type selection, and axis attribute filters arranged vertically with dropdown menus stacked with consistent spacing (about 16px). The top-level container has a horizontal header bar including the application name on the left and user avatar on the right. The overall grid system uses vertical stacking within each column and horizontal distribution between columns, balancing the space for navigation, content, and controls. The dropdown menus in the right column have nested grouping with scrolling capability. Margins and paddings are consistent, and typography aligns left in lists and controls. The layout keywords include three-column, vertical sidebar, filter sidebar, central content area, fixed width columns, dropdown filters, stacked vertical forms, responsive data visualization, and header navigation.\n- **Functions**: Users can navigate through the navigation sidebar to access different sections like Notifications, Tasks, Reports, and Records. On this screen, the primary function is viewing and managing data reports. Users can refresh data via the 'Refresh data' link above the chart, ensuring the displayed statistics are up to date. The central bar chart visually represents company counts by country, facilitating data analysis and comparison. Users can interact with the right sidebar filters; specifically, they can select the data source from an available list, choose the report type (such as bar chart or other formats), and set attributes for the X axis through dropdown menus. The expanded 'X axis' dropdown allows searching and selecting various data attributes, aiding customization of the data visualization. This setup supports workflows such as configuring reports, filtering and sorting data attributes, and analyzing business intelligence metrics. Overall, the screen enables users to generate, customize, and review data-driven reports to monitor company data, thereby supporting informed decision-making and business analysis.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 37\n- **Name**: Attio\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/37\n- **Domain**: attio.com\n- **Categories**: Business, Productivity, Project Management, Collaboration Tools\n- **Description**: The data-driven CRM"
